  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An optical observatory in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Challenges Research Fund (GCRF) supports cutting-edge research to address challenges faced by developing countries. The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We will be working with colleagues in Kenya and South Africa to look at the ways in which a new optical astronomical observatory in Kenya can act as a catalyst to help develop an interest in STEM (Science Technology Engineering and Medicine) subjects and careers while at the same time providing astronomers in Kenya with a research facility that can be used by staff and students. An observatory can also provide a focus for developing new expertise in technology companies in Kenya by working with researchers to build instruments and observatory infrastructure. This will be done during 3 workshops where experience and expertise will be shared and a prospectus for an observatory drwn up</narrative>
  </description>
